From 7fb296381e217700cfa20065ab1557a2eb29d06a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:03:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fork: keep the composer usable during voice mode

The text box stays editable in realtime voice mode (typing, paste, drafts
survive), and the full-card overlay is replaced by a voice strip at the
top of the composer card: mini volume meter, status label (Connecting,
Listening, Thinking, Speaking, Muted, Ending), Mute and End. On desktop
Mute is a labeled pill with a Space-bar hint while the text box is not
focused; on compact it is an icon button so every locale fits at 375px.
The toolbar mic is hidden in voice mode, and starting voice from the
AudioLines button exits fullscreen so the strip is visible. Adds a
voice-strip design to the design frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
